## Purpose

Activate the read-only Project Activity route landed in #1608 on the same Convex-backed API surface that already serves project correspondence.

## Change

- mount `createProjectActivityApi()` inside `createApiV1()` only when the work ledger is `ConvexWorkLedger`;
- build both live read sources from the ledger's existing Convex client, service secret, and workspace;
- leave SQLite/local API behavior unchanged;
- preserve the route's existing project/read auth fence, bounded limit, zero-authority projection, and source-completeness envelope.

## Proof

A focused API-v1 integration control proves that one authenticated `/projects/stensibly/activity?limit=12` request:

- reaches exactly `mailCorrespondence:listProjectSources` and `orchestratorActivity:listRecentObservations`;
- sends identical service-secret/workspace/project/limit scope to both reads;
- produces `project-activity/v1` with zero authority/effects;
- preserves correspondence degradation counts independently from orchestrator truncation;
- performs no mutation.

The `api-v1.ts` diff is intentionally tiny: 19 additive lines (two imports + one Convex-only route mount). No existing route or error behavior is changed.

## Validation note

The first head exposed a test-fixture typo: the mock expected `correspondence:listProject`, while the existing live source correctly calls `mailCorrespondence:listProjectSources`. Production mount code was unchanged; the control now names the real query and exact-head CI is rerunning.

## Boundary

Hosted activation + one integration control only. No UI, no provider call, no new persistence, no causal inference, no activity mutation, no reply/action composer.

Refs #1586, #1608, #1607, #1582.

